    {"topic": "notification", "text": "2200 m (135.7-137.8 kHz): the operating site must be notified to BNetzA in writing or electronically before use, the transmit antenna must be adequately decoupled from other installations, and operation must stop if it interferes with a primary service, including in a neighbouring band. Row 1 only (row 2, 630 m, does not carry this condition). Shown, not enforced.", "src": "D1 Anl.1 B2 p.11"}
